; TS2Python.def — force undecorated export names for EL's DefineDLLFunc.
;
; Why: on x86 with __stdcall + __declspec(dllexport), MSVC decorates exports
; as _Name@N (e.g. _EL_Init@4). EasyLanguage's DefineDLLFunc / GetProcAddress
; looks up the raw "EL_Init" name and fails. Listing exports here makes the
; linker emit them under the plain symbol name while keeping the __stdcall
; call convention intact.
;
; Keep this in sync with include/ts2python.h.
;
; EL_PublishTick and EL_PublishBar are TOMBSTONES — they return -6 and
; publish nothing. Keep them listed: dropping an export makes an .ELD built
; against the superseded protocol fail at DefineDLLFunc resolution with no
; explanation, whereas -6 puts a readable line in TradeStation's Print Log.
; See ../contract/error_codes.md.
;
; EL_Init2 and EL_Init3 are GONE, and EL_Init now takes five parameters
; instead of the one the superseded protocol's EL_Init took. That reuse is
; deliberate and it is a hazard: __stdcall has the callee pop the arguments,
; so an .ELD still bound to the one-argument EL_Init resolves this export,
; calls it, and corrupts the stack. Nothing on this side can detect it. The
; DLL and the .ELD are one unit — install and re-Verify them together.

LIBRARY TS2Python
EXPORTS
    EL_Init
    EL_Publish
    EL_PublishTick
    EL_PublishBar
    EL_Shutdown
    EL_DllVersion
